  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the status of drive 8 from channel 15 (TALK, TKSA $6f). The bytes up to the second comma go to drive_status_text: the error number, a space for the first comma, and the message. Then it skips the rest up to the CR. C is clear when the number is 00; then SA is restored. When no device answers (STATUS not 0 after TALK), the script at $2e0a writes DEVICE NOT PRESENT at $c7d1, and C is set."},
    {"at":25,"placement":"side","text":"script_flag = 0: no comma yet. The text index 0 goes on the stack."},
    {"at":43,"placement":"side","text":"First comma: script_flag = $20, and a space goes into the text."},
    {"at":69,"placement":"side","text":"The error number 00: no error."}
  ],
